WEBVTT

00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:17,100
I'm a new rife user. I have a daily overnight program and also three shorter daytime programs.

00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:23,500
Which should I run if I have time during the day? Can I tell how long the day programs are?

00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:29,580
So the daytime programs, they're not in order or anything. Your overnight programs aren't

00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:34,220
in any order whatsoever either. Does it make a difference if, oh,

00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:41,980
shoot today's Wednesday and I realized I ran Thursday's program. So what? Then just run Wednesdays

00:00:41,980 --> 00:00:45,500
tomorrow or just run Thursdays again tomorrow. It doesn't make any difference.

00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:52,620
Oh, which day program should I run? It doesn't make any difference. So just start with the first one.

00:00:53,660 --> 00:00:59,580
They can be, you know, I don't remember on everybody's program how long they are, but as soon as you

00:01:00,380 --> 00:01:05,820
open up that program and hit run, you'll see the countdown timer. So you'll see how long the

00:01:05,820 --> 00:01:10,860
program is. So what if it's two hours and I only have an hour? Just run it for an hour then.

00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:18,300
You know, what if it's, you know, what if I only have 15 minutes? Just run it for 15 minutes then

00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:24,460
and turn off if you have to get up and go do something and you're not coming back. There's nothing

00:01:24,540 --> 00:01:30,220
wrong with that. There's no wrong way to do it. There's no wrong, there's no wrong way to run any

00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:36,060
of your programs. So don't, don't get hung up on thinking you have to do those things

00:01:36,860 --> 00:01:45,820
right. The wrong way to do it is to not do it. So that's the wrong way to do it. So you just want to

00:01:45,820 --> 00:01:52,460
run those programs. When I was in the thick of my cancer, I was running literally, I've said this

00:01:53,420 --> 00:01:59,340
dozens of times. I'd get home and sit in my chair. I had the right right there and I turned it

00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:05,020
on and I was running my program. If I got up to go eat or got up to go do something, I just let it

00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:10,380
run and I came back and sit down. Sometimes it was five minutes later. Sometimes it was an hour later.

00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:19,020
It was just running my whole overnight program. So I ran my overnight program. So as I got home and

00:02:19,820 --> 00:02:24,620
when I was ready to go to bed, I turned it off and turned it back on and ran my overnight program

00:02:24,620 --> 00:02:31,020
all night long. And then when I went to work, I was running the rife all day at work. Now,

00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:35,020
I wasn't always sitting at my desk, but when I was sitting at my desk, I was getting the frequencies,

00:02:35,020 --> 00:02:39,660
but then I'd get up and go help people and go do things and I came back and sat at my desk and I was

00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:46,300
running the rife program all day long. So I was getting as much rife time as possible. But

00:02:46,940 --> 00:02:52,700
you know, again, I was in a situation where there wasn't any other hope for me with my cancer.

00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:59,420
So I just, I had to hit this as hard as I possibly could. So I just think the more rife time you get

00:02:59,420 --> 00:03:04,860
the better. Within reason, I don't want you to not live your life because you have to do the rife.

00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:09,900
I want, you know, if you have to go play with the grandkids, go be with the grandkids. But, you know,

00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:16,620
you want to, well, you're sitting and doing nothing, reading a book or so either watching TV or

00:03:16,620 --> 00:03:22,540
rather be running the rife set up your house that you can do that. And that's there's no wrong way

00:03:22,540 --> 00:03:31,180
to do it if you're doing it if you're just running the programs.

